David Jacot resolved KAFKA-15237.
---------------------------------
    Fix Version/s: 3.7.0
       Resolution: Fixed

> Implement write operation timeout
> ---------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-15237
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15237
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Sub-task
>            Reporter: David Jacot
>            Assignee: Sagar Rao
>            Priority: Major
>              Labels: kip-848-preview
>             Fix For: 3.7.0
>
>
> In the scala code, we rely on `offsets.commit.timeout.ms` to bound all the writes. We should do the same in the new code. This is important to ensure that the number of pending response in the purgatory is bound. The name of the config is not ideal but we should keep it for backward compatibility reasons.



